-- flash_highlight briefly flashes an element's background, to point the reader at it.  Calling it
-- again while a flash is running restarts the flash.  Styled by .flash-highlight in 02-animations.css
def flash_highlight(node)

	if no node then
		exit
	end

	-- The animation runs once and ends on the normal background, so the class can stay afterwards.
	-- RULE: never wait for animationend here; a waiting `on click` queues every later click behind it.
	-- Removing the class and reading a layout property restarts the animation on a second call
	remove .flash-highlight from node
	get node.offsetWidth
	add .flash-highlight to node
end
